Z||000013||Dave Gunsul||07-25-2001||01:13 PM||||I've got the blue headlights from them and they are pretty cool. I think that Fierofreek is talking about foglights which are a completely different thing. The headlights come in blue and gold.<P>I also have not had any trouble with them and i have order quite a bit. The prices aren't really that bad especially when you get a club discount.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BTW not trying to rub it in just relating my experiences with them.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000014||Fformula88||07-25-2001||04:36 PM||||I have had a couple mix ups with them, but they are more than willing to correct any mistake they make.  I know it can be annoying when you get a mixed up order, but most places are pure hell to try and get it straightened out.  They do it right away.<P>I think they run a great operation overall, and they offer a lot of parts that would be hard to find, or impossible to find otherwise.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Toddster||07-25-2001||04:56 PM||||I've gotta say that they have typically been the best Fiero Parts supplier I've ever dealt with.<P>But at this time of year, with all the car shows, many people wait til the last minute and orders can get mixed-up because they are so busy. ||||reg||1
